WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.123
Worked example: all Northstar figures are synthetic, in USD thousands, for the same quarter.

00:00:06.363 --> 00:00:07.856
Revenue is 600.

00:00:08.096 --> 00:00:13.600
Operating expenses excluding depreciation and amortization are 420.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.912
Depreciation is 30; amortization is 10.

00:00:17.152 --> 00:00:21.013
There is no other operating or non-operating income or expense.

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:27.205
Interest expense is 20, there is no interest income, and income-tax expense is 36.

00:00:27.895 --> 00:00:34.615
Top down: 600 − 420 − 30 − 10 = 140 EBIT.

00:00:34.855 --> 00:00:39.677
Then 140 − 20 − 36 = 84 net income.

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:47.620
Bottom up: 84 net income + 20 interest + 36 income tax = 140 EBIT.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:53.321
Add 30 depreciation + 10 amortization = 180 EBITDA.

00:00:53.561 --> 00:00:56.761
The bridge difference is 96, not a cash deposit.

00:00:57.001 --> 00:01:02.591
Check: 180 − 30 − 10 − 20 − 36 = 84.

00:01:03.281 --> 00:01:07.398
EBITDA = EBIT + depreciation + amortization.

00:01:07.638 --> 00:01:17.089
In this simplified case, EBITDA = net income + interest expense + income-tax expense + depreciation + amortization.

00:01:17.329 --> 00:01:20.230
All add-backs were already deducted in net income.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:30.198
If a statement contains interest income, use the disclosed interest treatment consistently; removing net interest means adding expense and subtracting income.

00:01:30.438 --> 00:01:34.705
Other non-operating items can make EBIT different from operating income.

00:01:34.945 --> 00:01:37.078
Do not assume those terms always match.

00:01:37.768 --> 00:01:41.416
Take two minutes to rebuild the bridge on paper before continuing.

00:01:41.656 --> 00:01:44.173
The figures and calculations are original.

00:01:44.863 --> 00:01:45.951
Now it's your turn.

00:01:46.191 --> 00:01:58.309
A second synthetic quarter has net income 50, interest expense 12, income-tax expense 18 and D&A 25, all in USD thousands.

00:01:58.549 --> 00:01:59.701
What is EBITDA?

